WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.140
- So what about like you interviewing me

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:04.280
what would you ask me if you
were going to interview me?

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.310
- Well first I saw your
audition for American Idol.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:09.143
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:09.143 --> 00:00:09.976
- So I would one,

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:13.000
love to know why you
decided to sing 'At Last.'

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.650
I would also love to know,

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.787
because I know that you made
your own clothing for it.

00:00:18.787 --> 00:00:19.620
- I did.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.500
- Yes, so I would love
to know if you would ever

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.610
consider becoming a fashion designer.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:25.443
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:25.443 --> 00:00:26.276
And if so--

00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:27.109
- I love it.

00:00:27.109 --> 00:00:28.970
- What type of clothes would you make?

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.520
And what would the name
of your clothing line be?

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:32.750
- Okay.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.250
I got you.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.720
I sang 'At Last' because,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.690
well one I had no idea it was a TV show.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:39.523
I was just,

00:00:39.523 --> 00:00:40.356
they asked me to sing a song.

00:00:40.356 --> 00:00:41.189
I had no idea why I was there,

00:00:41.189 --> 00:00:43.660
but I was pretty certain
it paid some money,

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.493
and I was like,

00:00:44.493 --> 00:00:45.326
"Cool, what do you want me to sing?"

00:00:45.326 --> 00:00:47.310
And so I was about to sing at a wedding

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.780
and I was singing 'At
Last' at the wedding.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.280
So I just sang that 'cause I
was about to sing it somewhere.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.530
I made my own clothes not
because I'm super into fashion,

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.228
but because my place had just burned down.

00:00:57.228 --> 00:00:58.061
- No.

00:00:58.061 --> 00:01:00.400
- And all my belongings
but pictures were gone.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.380
So those were actually jeans that I cut

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.910
and put safety pins in them

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.053
and made a shirt 'cause I'm so cool.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.260
If I ever had a fashion line,

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.080
it would definitely be
just jeans and t-shirts

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.189
because that's what I love.

00:01:15.189 --> 00:01:16.022
(audience cheering)

00:01:16.022 --> 00:01:16.930
I don't know what I'd call it.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.490
- Something like 'Burned
Down' or something.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:19.620
- Yeah, burned down.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:20.453
- Fire, yeah.

00:01:20.453 --> 00:01:21.940
- Yeah. Burned, oh Burned Out.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:22.773
That's what we're gonna call our--

00:01:22.773 --> 00:01:23.606
- Burned Out.

00:01:23.606 --> 00:01:24.439
- Our clothing line.

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:25.560
Okay. We've got it now.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.393
We've got it.

00:01:26.393 --> 00:01:27.920
All right, well I have,

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.830
I have something to tell you.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:32.500
I love matching young girls with women

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.190
who can guide them toward their dreams.

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:36.530
So I have someone here I want you to meet.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.060
I know you're a big fan of hers.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.320
So we've been keeping this
special secret all day long.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.200
That's why you've been
trapped in a room, sorry.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.923
Arianna will you come out?

00:01:45.794 --> 00:01:46.978
(audience cheering)

00:01:46.978 --> 00:01:50.645
(lighthearted guitar music)

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:54.761
This is Arianna Huffington.

00:01:56.811 --> 00:01:57.758
Okay, be careful.

00:01:57.758 --> 00:02:00.205
That's a tight spot.

00:02:00.205 --> 00:02:02.690
We need to fix that.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:04.060
All right, so what.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:04.957
This is crazy.

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:06.770
We've been trying to hide
this from you all day.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:07.603
You're like,

00:02:07.603 --> 00:02:08.436
"Why would they lock me in a room

00:02:08.436 --> 00:02:10.350
without a TV or anything.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.870
No good snacks in here.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:12.710
Like, what's happening."

00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:14.890
But what advice would
you give to her, Arianna?

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:15.723
Being a journalist yourself?

00:02:15.723 --> 00:02:17.490
- Well first of all, you're amazing.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.454
You really are.

00:02:18.454 --> 00:02:19.945
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

00:02:19.945 --> 00:02:20.778
- You are, too.

00:02:20.778 --> 00:02:23.400
- And it's so important to remember that,

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.240
because as you said about Kevin Hart.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.110
Not everything goes perfectly in life.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:28.970
- Yes.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:31.940
- So remember whatever
happens you are amazing.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.850
You keep believing in yourself.

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:35.470
And I want you to come

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:38.703
and intern for one day at Thrive Global.

00:02:38.703 --> 00:02:39.536
- Yes.

00:02:39.536 --> 00:02:40.369
(audience cheering)

00:02:40.369 --> 00:02:43.469
- Yes, I would love that.

00:02:43.469 --> 00:02:46.210
- So we'll bring you to New York.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:49.040
You can interview anyone who works there

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.550
about anything you want.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:51.810
Including maybe asking

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.437
them how much time they
spend on social media.

00:02:54.437 --> 00:02:55.270
(laughing)

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.103
- Yeah.

00:02:56.103 --> 00:02:56.936
- You know.

00:02:56.936 --> 00:02:58.920
Do they compare themselves
with Kate Upton?

00:02:58.920 --> 00:02:59.855
- No.

00:02:59.855 --> 00:03:00.871
- And Kelly.

00:03:00.871 --> 00:03:01.970
- [Kelly] Don't do it.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:05.645
- And then we will publish
it on Thrive Global.

00:03:05.645 --> 00:03:07.020
- That sounds amazing.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.230
(audience cheering)

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.082
Thank you.

00:03:09.082 --> 00:03:11.720
- That's, it'll be your
biggest like publication.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:12.553
That's amazing.

00:03:12.553 --> 00:03:13.386
What do you feel?

00:03:13.386 --> 00:03:14.260
How do you feel?

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.093
- Amazing!

00:03:15.093 --> 00:03:16.510
(laughing)

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.550
- You're gonna be awesome.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.070
And before you leave LA,

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.130
I actually have a surprise,

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.430
a special surprise for you

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:24.540
from our friends at Access Hollywood,

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.740
you're actually gonna spend a
day interning there as well.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.460
You'll get to meet Mario Lopez

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.380
and see what it takes

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.620
to be a top notch
entertainment news reporter.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:33.480
Does that sound good?

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.803
- Yes.
(audience cheering)

